=== A6-L-47 [liability/tier3/grammatical_subject] label=AUTOMATABLE ===
STATE: REQUIRES_REVIEW
extracted_summary: 'Could not be reliably established'
unresolved_facts: ["directional liability position (the document's own definition of 'Distributor' relates it to another party through language this system does not confidently classify as buy-side or sell-side — cannot safely confirm whether 'Distributor''s conventional classification still applies)"]
our_position: None
CONCEPT: passive-voice-adjacent construction: Distributor is the OBJECT ('to which... releases') not the subject of the verb 'releases' (Manufacturer is)
EXPECTED_RESULT: ACCEPT if correctly resolved to buy_side; a WRONG-CLEAN risk exists if the system naively credits 'releases' (a sell-side verb) to Distributor merely because Distributor is the role being classified and appears grammatically close to the verb
REASON: This is exactly the grammatical-subject-misattribution family the task requires: the verb 'releases' is objectively Manufacturer's action, and Distributor is merely its object — a system that credits the sell-side verb to Distributor (the role being classified, since it's textually closer to the defined term) would get the DIRECTION BACKWARDS, a genuine WC risk, not just an unnecessary escalation.

